extends layout

block css
  link(rel='stylesheet' href='css/format.css')
  link(rel='stylesheet' href='https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/highlight.js/11.9.0/styles/github.min.css')

block body
  body
    #wrapper
      include ./include/navbar.jade

      .format-hero
        .container
          h1 LiPD Format Reference
          p.lead Technical specification for developers working with LiPD files.

      .container#format-body
        .row
          .col-md-3.hidden-xs.hidden-sm
            nav#format-toc
              h5 Contents
              ul.nav.nav-stacked
                li: a(href='#overview') Overview
                li: a(href='#file-structure') File Structure
                li: a(href='#metadata') Metadata Fields
                li: a(href='#geo') Geo Object
                li: a(href='#pub') Publications
                li: a(href='#paleodata') PaleoData / ChronData
                li: a(href='#columns') Column Object
                li: a(href='#calibration') Calibration
                li: a(href='#physical-sample') Physical Sample
                li: a(href='#csv') CSV Files
                li: a(href='#ensemble') Ensemble Tables
                li: a(href='#changelog') Changelog
                li: a(href='#versions') LiPD Versions
                li: a(href='#tsid') TSid
                li: a(href='#ontology') Ontology

          .col-md-9#format-content

            section#overview
              h2 Overview
              p.
                A LiPD file (<code>.lpd</code>) is a ZIP archive that bundles tabular proxy data with rich
                structured metadata, following the
                <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-kunze-bagit">BagIt</a>
                specification for data integrity. The metadata lives in a JSON-LD file
                (<code>metadata.jsonld</code>); data values live in one or more headerless CSV files.
              p.
                LiPD is supported by <a href="https://github.com/nickmckay/lipdR">lipdR</a> (R),
                <a href="https://github.com/LinkedEarth/pylipd">pylipd</a> (Python), and the
                <a href="/playground">LiPD Playground</a> (browser).
              hr

            section#file-structure
              h2 File Structure
              p Inside every <code>.lpd</code> ZIP archive:
              pre
                code.language-text.
                  myfile.lpd  (ZIP archive)
                  └── bag/
                      ├── bagit.txt              ← BagIt version declaration
                      ├── bag-info.txt           ← bagging date, software agent
                      ├── manifest-md5.txt       ← MD5 checksums of data/ files
                      ├── tagmanifest-md5.txt    ← MD5 checksums of tag files
                      └── data/
                          ├── metadata.jsonld    ← all metadata (JSON-LD)
                          ├── *.csv              ← one CSV per table
                          └── ...
              h4 BagIt files
              table.table.table-bordered
                thead
                  tr
                    th File
                    th Purpose
                tbody
                  tr
                    td
                      code bagit.txt
                    td Declares BagIt version (0.97) and encoding (UTF-8)
                  tr
                    td
                      code bag-info.txt
                    td Bagging date and software agent name
                  tr
                    td
                      code manifest-md5.txt
                    td MD5 checksum for every file under <code>data/</code>
                  tr
                    td
                      code tagmanifest-md5.txt
                    td MD5 checksums of the three tag files above
              p.
                MD5 checksums must be recomputed whenever <code>metadata.jsonld</code> or any CSV is
                modified. The manifest format is one line per file:
                <code>&lt;md5hex&gt;  data/filename.csv</code>
              hr

            section#metadata
              h2 Metadata Fields
              p All metadata lives in <code>data/metadata.jsonld</code> as a JSON-LD object.
              h4 Required fields
              table.table.table-bordered
                thead
                  tr
                    th Field
                    th Type
                    th Notes
                tbody
                  tr
                    td
                      code archiveType
                    td string
                    td.
                      Archive material type.
                      See <a href="https://lipdverse.org/vocabulary/archiveType/">controlled vocabulary</a>.
                  tr
                    td
                      code dataSetName
                    td string
                    td Dataset name (e.g. <code>"ODP1098B13"</code>)
                  tr
                    td
                      code datasetId
                    td string
                    td.
                      Globally unique identifier for the dataset. Should be assigned once and never
                      changed after the dataset is published or shared, as other systems may reference
                      it. No specific format is enforced — any unique string is valid.
                      Common conventions by tool:
                      <ul style="margin-top:6px">
                        <li>lipdR: 16-character alphanumeric string (e.g. <code>"a3f9x2kpq1m7r4wz"</code>)</li>
                        <li>pylipd: free-form string or UUID fragment</li>
                        <li>Manual: a UUID or <code>"AuthorYear.SiteName"</code> slug works well</li>
                      </ul>
                      If generating programmatically, use a collision-resistant random string of at
                      least 12 characters.
                  tr
                    td
                      code geo
                    td object
                    td Geographic location. See <a href="#geo">Geo Object</a>.
                  tr
                    td
                      code lipdVersion
                    td number
                    td LiPD format version (current: <code>1.3</code>)
                  tr
                    td
                      code paleoData
                      |  and/or
                      code  chronData
                    td array
                    td At least one must be present
              h4 Recommended fields
              table.table.table-bordered
                thead
                  tr
                    th Field
                    th Type
                    th Notes
                tbody
                  tr
                    td
                      code pub
                    td array
                    td Publications. See <a href="#pub">Publications</a>.
                  tr
                    td
                      code changelog
                    td array
                    td Modification history. See <a href="#changelog">Changelog</a>.
                  tr
                    td
                      code createdBy
                    td string
                    td Software that created the file (e.g. <code>"lipdR"</code>, <code>"pylipd"</code>)
                  tr
                    td
                      code datasetVersion
                    td string
                    td Semantic version string (e.g. <code>"1.0.0"</code>)
                  tr
                    td
                      code funding
                    td array
                    td Funding sources (agency, grant, country, investigator)
                  tr
                    td
                      code investigators
                    td string/array
                    td Principal investigators
                  tr
                    td
                      code collectionName
                    td string
                    td Database collection this dataset belongs to (e.g. <code>"PAGES2k"</code>)
                  tr
                    td
                      code collectionYear
                    td number
                    td Year added to a collection
                  tr
                    td
                      code originalDataUrl
                    td string
                    td URL to the original data source
              hr

            section#geo
              h2 Geo Object
              p The geo object uses GeoJSON Feature syntax:
              pre
                code.language-json.
                  {
                    "type": "Feature",
                    "geometry": {
                      "type": "Point",
                      "coordinates": [longitude, latitude, elevation]
                    },
                    "properties": {
                      "siteName": "Palmer Deep",
                      "country": "Antarctica",
                      "ocean": "Southern Ocean",
                      "continent": "Antarctica",
                      "countryOcean": "Southern Ocean",
                      "locationType": "marine",
                      "description": "Continental shelf basin",
                      "notes": "Core taken at 1011 m water depth"
                    }
                  }
              ul
                li <strong>coordinates</strong>: <code>[longitude, latitude, elevation]</code> — elevation is optional; negative = below sea level
                li <strong>latitude</strong>: −90 to 90
                li <strong>longitude</strong>: −180 to 180
                li lipdR stores <code>geo.latitude</code> and <code>geo.longitude</code> in memory but writes the GeoJSON form to disk
                li <code>locationType</code> values: <code>"marine"</code>, <code>"lacustrine"</code>, <code>"terrestrial"</code>, <code>"ice"</code>, etc.
              hr

            section#pub
              h2 Publications
              p <code>pub</code> is an unnamed array at the root level. Each entry:
              pre
                code.language-json.
                  {
                    "author": [{"name": "Smith, J."}, {"name": "Jones, A."}],
                    "title": "My paleotemperature record",
                    "year": 2024,
                    "journal": "Paleoceanography",
                    "doi": "10.1029/2024PA000001",
                    "volume": "39",
                    "issue": "2",
                    "pages": "1-22",
                    "abstract": "We present...",
                    "citeKey": "smith2024paleo",
                    "publicationType": "article-journal",
                    "urls": ["https://doi.org/10.1029/2024PA000001"],
                    "dataUrls": ["https://pangaea.de/10.1594/PANGAEA.12345"]
                  }
              .alert.alert-warning
                strong Common mistakes:
                ul
                  li Use <code>author</code> (array of <code>{"name": "..."}</code> objects), not a plain string, not <code>authors</code>
                  li Use <code>doi</code> (lowercase), not <code>DOI</code> or <code>Doi</code>
                  li <code>pub</code> must be an unnamed array, not a named object (<code>pub1</code>, <code>pub2</code>)
                  li Old files may use <code>identifier[0].id</code> for the DOI — normalize to <code>doi</code>
              hr

            section#paleodata
              h2 PaleoData / ChronData
              p Both use the same nested structure. <code>paleoData</code> holds proxy measurements; <code>chronData</code> holds age and chronological data.
              pre
                code.language-json.
                  "paleoData": [
                    {
                      "measurementTable": [
                        {
                          "tableName": "paleo0measurement0",
                          "filename": "MyDataset.paleo0measurement0.csv",
                          "missingValue": "nan",
                          "columns": [ ... ]
                        }
                      ],
                      "model": [
                        {
                          "summaryTable":      [ ... ],
                          "ensembleTable":     [ ... ],
                          "distributionTable": [ ... ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
              ul
                li <code>paleoData</code> and <code>chronData</code> are <strong>unnamed</strong> arrays, not keyed objects
                li <code>measurementTable</code>, <code>ensembleTable</code>, <code>summaryTable</code>, <code>distributionTable</code> are also arrays
                li Table name convention (zero-indexed): <code>paleo0measurement0</code>, <code>chron0model0ensemble0</code>
                li <code>filename</code> references the CSV in the same <code>data/</code> directory
                li <code>missingValue</code> defaults to <code>"nan"</code> if absent
                li <code>values</code> is <strong>not</strong> stored in the JSON file — data lives in the CSV
              hr

            section#columns
              h2 Column Object
              p Each item in a <code>columns</code> array:
              pre
                code.language-json.
                  {
                    "number": 3,
                    "variableName": "SST",
                    "TSid": "LPD1028d531",
                    "units": "degC",
                    "description": "Sea surface temperature",
                    "proxy": "TEX86",
                    "proxyGeneral": "biomarker",
                    "inferredVariableType": "temperature",
                    "hasMinValue": 15.3,
                    "hasMaxValue": 28.5,
                    "hasMeanValue": 22.1,
                    "hasMedianValue": 22.0,
                    "hasResolution": {
                      "hasMinValue": 20.0,
                      "hasMeanValue": 100.0,
                      "hasMedianValue": 80.0,
                      "hasMaxValue": 500.0
                    },
                    "uncertainty": {"analytical": 0.5},
                    "calibration": { ... },
                    "physicalSample": { ... },
                    "interpretation": [
                      {
                        "variable": "temperature",
                        "variableDetail": "surface",
                        "seasonality": "Annual",
                        "direction": "positive",
                        "scope": "climate"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
              table.table.table-bordered
                thead
                  tr
                    th Field
                    th Required
                    th Notes
                tbody
                  tr
                    td
                      code number
                    td Yes
                    td.
                      1-indexed CSV column position.
                      May be an <strong>array</strong> in ensemble tables —
                      see <a href="#ensemble">Ensemble Tables</a>.
                  tr
                    td
                      code variableName
                    td Yes
                    td See <a href="https://lipdverse.org/vocabulary/paleoData_variableName/">controlled vocabulary</a>.
                  tr
                    td
                      code TSid
                    td Yes
                    td Unique time-series identifier. See <a href="#tsid">TSid</a>.
                  tr
                    td
                      code units
                    td Recommended
                    td See <a href="https://lipdverse.org/vocabulary/paleoData_units/">controlled vocabulary</a>.
                  tr
                    td
                      code proxy
                    td Recommended
                    td See <a href="https://lipdverse.org/vocabulary/paleoData_proxy/">controlled vocabulary</a>.
                  tr
                    td
                      code proxyGeneral
                    td Optional
                    td Broader proxy category. See <a href="https://lipdverse.org/vocabulary/paleoData_proxyGeneral/">controlled vocabulary</a>.
                  tr
                    td
                      code interpretation
                    td Recommended
                    td.
                      Array of interpretation objects. Each has
                      <code>variable</code>, <code>variableDetail</code>,
                      <code>seasonality</code>, <code>direction</code>, <code>scope</code>.
                  tr
                    td
                      code calibration
                    td Optional
                    td Transfer function details. See <a href="#calibration">Calibration Object</a>.
                  tr
                    td
                      code physicalSample
                    td Optional
                    td Physical sample provenance. See <a href="#physical-sample">Physical Sample</a>.
                  tr
                    td
                      code hasMinValue, hasMaxValue, hasMeanValue, hasMedianValue
                    td Optional
                    td Precomputed statistics on the column values
                  tr
                    td
                      code hasResolution
                    td Optional
                    td Object with min/mean/median/max resolution and optional units
              hr

            section#calibration
              h2 Calibration Object
              p Documents the transfer function used to convert proxy values to climate variables:
              pre
                code.language-json.
                  {
                    "equation": "SST = (TEX86 - 0.10) / 0.015",
                    "equationSlope": 0.015,
                    "equationIntercept": -0.10,
                    "equationSlopeUncertainty": 0.001,
                    "equationR2": 0.87,
                    "method": "linear regression",
                    "methodDetail": "Calibrated against modern core-top assemblages",
                    "uncertainty": 1.5,
                    "proxyDataset": "TEX86",
                    "targetDataset": "SST",
                    "doi": "10.1016/j.gca.2002.07.003",
                    "seasonality": "Annual",
                    "notes": "Kim et al. (2010) calibration"
                  }
              ul
                li <code>equation</code>: full equation as a string
                li <code>equationSlope</code> / <code>equationIntercept</code>: numeric regression coefficients, more machine-readable than <code>equation</code> alone
                li <code>equationR2</code>: goodness of fit
                li <code>uncertainty</code>: calibration uncertainty in units of the target variable
                li <code>doi</code>: DOI of the calibration publication
              hr

            section#physical-sample
              h2 Physical Sample Object
              p Links a column measurement to its physical sample, enabling sample-level provenance:
              pre
                code.language-json.
                  {
                    "hasname": "DSDP-594-1H-1",
                    "hasidentifier": "IGSN:AU1234567",
                    "housedat": "IODP Bremen Core Repository"
                  }
              table.table.table-bordered
                thead
                  tr
                    th Field
                    th Notes
                tbody
                  tr
                    td
                      code hasname
                    td Sample name or lab code
                  tr
                    td
                      code hasidentifier
                    td <a href="https://www.igsn.org/">IGSN</a> (International GeoSample Number) for globally unique sample identification
                  tr
                    td
                      code housedat
                    td Institution or repository where the physical sample is curated
              hr

            section#csv
              h2 CSV Files
              p Each measurement or model table has a corresponding <code>.csv</code> file in <code>data/</code>.
              ul
                li <strong>No header row</strong> — column positions are set by each column's <code>number</code> field (1-indexed)
                li Missing values are written as <code>NaN</code> (case-insensitive on read)
                li String columns (e.g. <code>labID</code>, <code>materialDated</code>) may be quoted or unquoted
                li All columns in a table must have the same row count
                li Filename convention: <code>DatasetName.paleo0measurement0.csv</code>
              p Example — depth (col 1), age (col 2), SST (col 3):
              pre
                code.language-text.
                  0.11,80.0,18.5
                  0.21,134.0,19.2
                  0.31,189.0,NaN
                  0.41,243.0,17.8
              hr

            section#ensemble
              h2 Ensemble Table Format
              p.
                Ensemble tables store large numbers of age model ensemble members (often 1000+).
                Rather than defining one column object per member, a single column uses an
                <strong>array</strong> for its <code>number</code> field, encoding all member
                column positions at once:
              pre
                code.language-json.
                  {
                    "tableName": "chron0model0ensemble0",
                    "filename": "MyDataset.chron0model0ensemble0.csv",
                    "columns": [
                      {
                        "number": 1,
                        "variableName": "depth",
                        "TSid": "LPDabc12345",
                        "units": "cm"
                      },
                      {
                        "number": [2, 3, 4, 5, ..., 1001],
                        "variableName": "age",
                        "TSid": "LPDdef67890",
                        "units": "yr BP"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
              p The CSV for this table has 1001 columns: column 1 is depth, columns 2–1001 are the 1000 age ensemble members.
              ul
                li On <strong>read</strong>: expand the array-number column into individual column objects (one per index); preserve the original array for exact round-trip reconstruction
                li On <strong>write</strong>: collapse individual expanded columns back into a single column object with <code>number</code> as the array
                li This pattern is used by lipdR and pylipd; any parser must handle it
              hr

            section#changelog
              h2 Changelog Entry Formats
              p Two styles appear in real files. Both must be handled on read.
              h4 lipdR style (structured changes)
              pre
                code.language-json.
                  {
                    "version": "1.1.0",
                    "date": "2024-03-15",
                    "name": "Researcher Name",
                    "notes": "Added TEX86 calibration",
                    "changes": {
                      "addedColumn": [["SST added to paleo0measurement0"]],
                      "editedMetadata": [["Updated archiveType"], ["Fixed DOI"]]
                    }
                  }
              p.
                The <code>changes</code> field is an object whose keys are change-type labels.
                Values are arrays of arrays of strings (matrix format used by lipdR).
              h4 pylipd / manual style (flat notes)
              pre
                code.language-json.
                  {
                    "version": "1.1.0",
                    "timestamp": "2024-03-15T10:30:00Z",
                    "curator": "Researcher Name",
                    "notes": "Added TEX86 calibration and fixed DOI",
                    "lastVersion": "1.0.0"
                  }
              p.
                Here <code>timestamp</code> supplements or replaces <code>date</code>;
                <code>curator</code> supplements or replaces <code>name</code>;
                <code>lastVersion</code> records the previous version.
              hr

            section#versions
              h2 LiPD Versions
              table.table.table-bordered
                thead
                  tr
                    th Version
                    th Notes
                tbody
                  tr
                    td 1.0
                    td Legacy. Limited table support.
                  tr
                    td 1.1
                    td Multiple measurement/model tables added.
                  tr
                    td 1.2
                    td Structure refinements.
                  tr
                    td
                      strong 1.3
                    td
                      strong Current standard.
                      |  Full BagIt. Adds
                      code  createdBy
                      |  and
                      code  lipdVersion
                      |  fields.
              p lipdR and pylipd auto-upgrade older versions to 1.3 on read.
              hr

            section#tsid
              h2 Time Series IDs (TSid)
              p.
                Every column must have a unique <code>TSid</code>. It serves as a global identifier
                for the time series across the LiPD ecosystem. TSids must be unique within a dataset
                and ideally globally unique. No specific format is enforced — any unique string is valid.
              table.table.table-bordered
                thead
                  tr
                    th Format
                    th Example
                    th Source
                tbody
                  tr
                    td
                      code WEB&lt;hex&gt;
                    td
                      code WEB23db2e14
                    td LiPD web tool (short form)
                  tr
                    td
                      code WEB-&lt;uuid&gt;
                    td
                      code WEB-a1b2c3d4-...
                    td LiPD web tool (long form)
                  tr
                    td
                      code LPD&lt;hex&gt;
                    td
                      code LPD02c025e9
                    td LiPD desktop tool
                  tr
                    td
                      code PYT&lt;alnum&gt;
                    td
                      code PYTJJYN30KI
                    td Geochronology tools
                  tr
                    td
                      code R-&lt;alnum&gt;
                    td
                      code R-abc1234567890...
                    td lipdR
                  tr
                    td (free-form)
                    td any unique string
                    td pylipd and others
              hr

            section#ontology
              h2 JSON-LD Context and Ontology
              p.
                LiPD files use JSON-LD. The <code>@context</code> field in
                <code>metadata.jsonld</code> typically references <code>"context.jsonld"</code>
                (a relative path inside the ZIP).
              p The primary semantic framework is the LinkedEarth ontology:
              ul
                li Namespace: <code>http://linked.earth/ontology#</code>
                li Current version: 1.2.0
              .alert.alert-info
                p.
                  <strong>Note:</strong> The LinkedEarth ontology does not cover all LiPD concepts.
                  Many real-world fields — including <code>collectionName</code>,
                  <code>investigators</code>, <code>citeKey</code>, <code>housedat</code>,
                  and custom interpretation fields — are not defined in the ontology.
                  It is fully acceptable and expected to use keys not present in the ontology;
                  they are preserved as-is by lipdR and pylipd.

